A||||6||AkursedX||Subwoofer Troubles||||5||
Z||000000||AkursedX||08-02-2000||03:59 PM||||Hello, I'm new to this forum and this is my 1st post.<P>I have an aftermarket radio/Cd player in my 88 Fiero GT (Kenwood KDC3011 to be exact), now I have everything hooked up properly, and I got the correct harnesses and everything, but I don't get anything out of the factory subwoofer.<BR>I was wondering if there is anything that I can do to get the subwoofer to work.  I figured all I would have to do is hook up the blue wire which is the power antenna/amp wire and it would be ok.<BR>So I'm kind of stumped right now.  Maybe it is the head unit that doesn't untilize the radio or something like that.  <BR>Any feedback would be appreciated, thanks.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||08-02-2000||04:09 PM||||I don't know the Kenwood system, but on my Pioneer I have to explicitely switch on the subwoofer. It's a setting on the unit itself.||||reg||1
Z||000002||b lo 0||08-02-2000||04:16 PM||||I have a Kenwood unit too, and you have to run preamps to an amp to the sub  The Kenwoods don't have the extra channel built in.  the blue wire you speak of is only to turn on the amp, not to send a signal to the amp.  You've got to run it from the RCA's.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">    <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||AkursedX||08-02-2000||04:25 PM||||Ok, so I have to run cable from the preamp outputs right to the amp?  So it's like a regular regular amp setup.  Well thank you for the feedback.<BR>I got a couple different options now.  I can either get a new head unit, and sell my old one with all my other stuff and get one that supports it.  Or else I can find someplace to cram my 250 watt amp and run the sub off of that along with the rear speakers.  I'll have to see.  <BR>Thank you again   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> <p>[This message has been edited by AkursedX (edited 08-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||08-02-2000||04:39 PM||||you have to splice the two pink wires from the subwoofer to the yellow wire from the car wiring harness coming into the adapter harness - the power antenna output is not enough to power the sub - believe me - I have been through this before..........just splice the two pinks to a wire which is hot with the ignition on (not on all the time) and it will work......<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/MY_SIGNATURE.gif">               <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||08-02-2000||04:50 PM||||I did what Tgowens said over last weekend and it sounds ok.. for a factory sub... My sub is signaled by an Alpine.||||reg||1
